1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,384
My toast always burns on the exact same corner, right at seven o'clock every single morning.

2
00:00:06,684 --> 00:00:13,092
I reach for the chipped yellow mug, feeling the exact same warmth against my tired fingertips.

3
00:00:13,392 --> 00:00:20,856
Outside the kitchen window, the same blue sparrow freezes mid-air, waiting for my permission to move.

4
00:00:21,156 --> 00:00:26,772
A sharp knock echoes from the front door, though nobody has visited me in ten years.

5
00:00:27,072 --> 00:00:32,928
I open the heavy wood, and find a digital receipt floating in the empty hallway air.

6
00:00:33,228 --> 00:00:41,556
Bold letters across the glowing screen read: Simulation complete. Customer rating four point nine stars.

7
00:00:41,856 --> 00:00:49,224
My entire childhood, my first heartbreak, this very kitchen—all of it was just an expensive memory pack.

8
00:00:49,524 --> 00:00:55,620
A bored tourist in the real world is about to take off their headset and forget me completely.

9
00:00:55,920 --> 00:01:02,304
My fingers start to dissolve into golden pixels, yet I still taste the bitter coffee on my tongue.

10
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:06,996
Would you pay to feel alive, if you knew the feeling was farmed?
